&lt;h2 id="tags-visualization-statistical"&gt;title: &amp;ldquo;Box/Violin Plot&amp;rdquo;
description: &amp;ldquo;Visualize data using either a Box Plot or a Violin Plot. Box plots are drawn as a box with a vertical line down the middle which is mean value, and has horizontal lines attached to each side (known as “whiskers”). Violin plots provide more detail by showing a smoothed density curve on each side, and also include a box plot inside for comparison.&amp;rdquo;
category: &amp;ldquo;Statistical&amp;rdquo;
operator_type: &amp;ldquo;BoxViolinPlot&amp;rdquo;
tags: [visualization, statistical]&lt;a class="td-heading-self-link" href="#tags-visualization-statistical" aria-label="Heading self-link"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
